# Notifications UX

The notification system is a core part of the product.

---

# Behavior

- Notifications are user-specific
- They are fetched via API
- Polling is used to detect updates

---

# Types

Examples:
- Document approved
- Document rejected
- Document assigned
- Document submitted

---

# UI Behavior

- Notifications appear in a dropdown (topbar)
- Show:
  - title
  - optional body
  - timestamp
- Group similar notifications

---

# Interaction

- Clicking a notification triggers its action
- Usually navigation to a specific entity

---

# Read State

- Notifications can be:
  - unread
  - read
- Users can:
  - mark individual as read
  - mark all as read

---

# Grouping

- Notifications are grouped by:
  - type
  - entity
  - date

---

# UX Principles

- Avoid overwhelming the user
- Show only relevant information
- Prioritize most recent activity